      "math_academy_id": "q-132768",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{2x+{y}^{3}}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{2x+{y}^{3}}}) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}((2x+{y}^{3})^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2x+{y}^{3})^{-3/2}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{(2x+{y}^{3})^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
